<title>SWITZERLAND: Sulzer wins order to equip Baxter plant.</title>
<headline>Sulzer wins order to equip Baxter plant.</headline>
<dateline>WINTERTHUR, Switzerland 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Engineering and medical technology group Sulzer Ag said its building services unit Sulzer Infra had won an order worth 16 million Swiss francs to equip a new pharmaceutical plant.</p>
<p>Sulzer said the order from U.S. company Baxter International Inc included heating, cooling and automation systems as well as so-called &quot;clean rooms&quot; for drug production at the plant being built in Neuchatel, Switzerland.</p>
<p>The work is due to be completed in the second quarter of this year, Sulzer said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Newsroom, +41-1-631 7340</p>
